<DocsLayout title="MyPaaS documentation" description="Install, deploy, configure, operate, and automate MyPaaS on a single Linux VM.">
<section><p class="overline">Overview</p><h2>What MyPaaS is</h2><p>MyPaaS is a self-hosted deployment control plane for one Linux server. It accepts Git repositories and public OCI images, operates container workloads through a Docker-compatible contract on Docker Engine or rootful Podman, and serves static releases directly through Caddy.</p><aside class="note"><p>These public docs describe current behavior on <code>main</code>. Roadmap and historical requirements are not presented as available features.</p></aside></section>
<section><h2>Deployment contracts</h2><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Dockerfile</strong></td><td>Build and run a Git repository Dockerfile.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Docker Compose</strong></td><td>Resolve multi-service Compose configuration and route the selected public service.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Static / SPA</strong></td><td>Build when needed, publish an atomic static release, and serve it through Caddy without a persistent app container.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Public OCI image</strong></td><td>Pull and run a compatible public registry image.</td></tr></tbody></table></section>
<section><h2>System model</h2><ol class="steps"><li>GitHub provides OAuth identity, repository access, and optional signed push events.</li><li>MyPaaS stores project configuration and deployment state and coordinates the deployment lifecycle.</li><li>Docker Engine or Podman provides the container runtime through the Docker-compatible command/socket contract.</li><li>Caddy routes container-backed projects and serves static releases.</li><li>Cloudflare Tunnel is the current production ingress path.</li></ol></section>
